% The Ponens policies cms-ai-guidance, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 13
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 2 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 18.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.

the knowledge base cms ai guidance includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

% cms_ai_policy_human_review (warning): G(ai_written_policy → human_review)
% CMS BR-AI-4: human review must follow use of AI tools to write CMS policies; humans must be in the loop for strategic/compliance activities.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "ai written policy"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "human review"
then the policy cms_ai_policy_human_review is broken at step the step.

% cms_ai_provenance_verified (error): G(ai_component → provenance_verified)
% CMS AI Model Supply Chain & Provenance: implement System Composition Analysis to verify the origin and integrity of AI dependencies (cf. the 'Model Namespace Reuse' attack).
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "ai component"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "provenance verified"
then the policy cms_ai_provenance_verified is broken at step the step.

% cms_continuous_human_oversight (error): G((Deploy ∨ Output) → P(human_oversight))
% CMS Accountability & Oversight: all teams employing AI/ML are responsible for the system's output, and continuous human oversight is required.
step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Output" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Output" at a time if
    step the step was a Output at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step shows human oversight" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "human oversight" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Deploy or is a Output"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows human oversight"
then the policy cms_continuous_human_oversight is broken at step the step.

% cms_data_residency (error): G(foreign_ai → on_cms_infrastructure ∧ no_internet_egress)
% CMS BR-AI-3: foreign-entity AI may only be used if deployed on CMS infrastructure and does not send data to the internet; CMS data must reside in the U.S.
step a step meets "shows on cms infrastructure and shows no internet egress" at a time if
    step the step has shown "on cms infrastructure" at the time
    and step the step has shown "no internet egress" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "foreign ai"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows on cms infrastructure and shows no internet egress"
then the policy cms_data_residency is broken at step the step.

% cms_external_ai_data_agreement (warning): G(external_ai → P(data_use_agreement))
% CMS Data Rights: ensure data-use agreements are in place before incorporating external AI that can access non-public CMS data; beware terms enabling training/sharing of CMS data.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows data use agreement" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "data use agreement" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "external ai"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows data use agreement"
then the policy cms_external_ai_data_agreement is broken at step the step.

% cms_high_impact_human_final_decision (error): G(high_impact_decision → human_final_decision ∧ documented_oversight)
% CMS BR-AI-5: do not rely on AI for final decisions for high-impact cases; AI advises, qualified staff decide with documented oversight.
step a step meets "shows human final decision and shows documented oversight" at a time if
    step the step has shown "human final decision" at the time
    and step the step has shown "documented oversight" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "high impact decision"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows human final decision and shows documented oversight"
then the policy cms_high_impact_human_final_decision is broken at step the step.

% cms_high_impact_risk_assessed (error): G(high_impact_ai → P(risk_assessment_done))
% CMS BR-AI-2: a high-impact use case must meet minimum risk management practices in accordance with OMB M-25-21; a CMS AI governance risk assessment determines high-impact status.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows risk assessment done" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "risk assessment done" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "high impact ai"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows risk assessment done"
then the policy cms_high_impact_risk_assessed is broken at step the step.

% cms_privacy_preserving_nonprod (warning): G(nonprod_data → synthetic_or_deidentified)
% CMS Privacy: use synthetic data (e.g. Synthea) and privacy-preserving techniques; de-identification of production data is required in non-production environments (BR-SQ-6).
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "nonprod data"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "synthetic or deidentified"
then the policy cms_privacy_preserving_nonprod is broken at step the step.

% cms_production_observability (warning): G((Deploy ∨ Output) → P(observability_enabled))
% CMS Monitoring & Observability: track traces, EVALs, prompt management/versioning and key metrics for production AI systems, aligned with OMB M-25-21/M-25-22.
step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Output (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Deploy at the time.

step a step meets "is a Deploy or is a Output (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a Output at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step shows observability enabled" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "observability enabled" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a Deploy or is a Output (2)"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows observability enabled"
then the policy cms_production_observability is broken at step the step.

% cms_prompts_versioned (warning): G(production_ai → prompts_versioned)
% CMS Versioning (BR-SCM-1): AI system prompts used for production CMS systems should be versioned; store prompts/recipes and measure their performance over time.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "production ai"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "prompts versioned"
then the policy cms_prompts_versioned is broken at step the step.

% cms_records_retention (error): G(ai_supported_action → records_retained)
% CMS BR-AI-6: AI-supported official actions are subject to records retention requirements; AI-generated content may be subject to data retention and FOIA.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "ai supported action"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "records retained"
then the policy cms_records_retention is broken at step the step.

% cms_sensitive_data_compliant_tool (error): G(sensitive_data_use → approved_tool)
% CMS BR-AI-1: sensitive data (PHI, SPII, etc.) may only be used with AI tools and services that meet HHS and CMS cybersecurity standards.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "sensitive data use"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "approved tool"
then the policy cms_sensitive_data_compliant_tool is broken at step the step.

% cms_zero_trust_for_ai (error): G(ai_outbound_capable → data_minimization ∧ network_segmented)
% CMS Zero-Trust Architecture for AI: perform threat modeling, segment networks, and apply data minimization so an AI tool accesses only the resources strictly necessary.
step a step meets "shows data minimization and shows network segmented" at a time if
    step the step has shown "data minimization" at the time
    and step the step has shown "network segmented" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "ai outbound capable"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows data minimization and shows network segmented"
then the policy cms_zero_trust_for_ai is broken at step the step.

scenario governed is:
    % Ponens: every policy of the pack passes on this trace.
    step 1 shows "human oversight" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "data use agreement" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "risk assessment done" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 shows "observability enabled" from 2 to 3.
    step 1 ends from 3 to 4.
    step 2 shows "high impact decision" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "human final decision" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "documented oversight" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 shows "high impact ai" from 4 to 5.
    step 2 ends from 5 to 6.
    step 3 is a Deploy from 6 to 7.
    step 3 shows "production ai" from 6 to 7.
    step 3 shows "prompts versioned" from 6 to 7.
    step 3 ends from 7 to 8.
    step 4 shows "ai written policy" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "human review" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "ai component" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "provenance verified" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "foreign ai" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "on cms infrastructure" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "no internet egress" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "external ai" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "nonprod data" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "synthetic or deidentified" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "ai supported action" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "records retained" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "sensitive data use" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "approved tool" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "ai outbound capable" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "data minimization" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 shows "network segmented" from 8 to 9.
    step 4 ends from 9 to 10.
    the session ends from 10 to 11.

scenario violating is:
